                        "entry_id": "7d43221f-a243-360e-b8a3-0cfdcb2742a0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An expression that gives information about the roots of a polynomial; for example, the expression D = b² - 4ac determines whether the roots of the quadratic equation ax² + bx + c = 0 are real and distinct (D > 0), real and equal (D = 0) or complex (D < 0)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6b28f296-18db-34c0-a9ed-6ea3896b7a7d",
                        "entry_id": "7d43221f-a243-360e-b8a3-0cfdcb2742a0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The invariant (on the vector space of forms of degree d in n variables) that vanishes exactly when the corresponding hypersurface in Pⁿ⁻¹ is singular."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
